+<p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Research resources</p><section><p class="eyebrow">VAP · RESEARCH RESOURCES</p><h1>Published research resources</h1><p class="lead">Choose evidence verification, mock controls or specification proposals by purpose.</p><div class="status"><p>Experimental extensions remain unadopted; independent third-party reproduction is not established. First-party CI and saved-evidence checks are separate from independent fresh execution.</p></div><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h2><a href="https://veritaschain.org/research/evidence-verification/">Choosing an evidence verifier or reproduction kit</a></h2><p>Select by purpose and environment: reviewing submitted evidence is separate from experimenting with execution controls and OS isolation.</p></article><article class="card"><h2><a href="https://veritaschain.org/research/cloud-credential-evidence/">Cloud credential and operation evidence research</a></h2><p>Synthetic research materials separate signature verification, authentication, operation authority and custody of records.</p></article><article class="card"><h2><a href="https://veritaschain.org/research/payment-authorization-evidence/">Payment API authorization and evidence research</a></h2><p>Mock experiments distinguish valid signatures, exact-request approval, known execution outcomes and retained evidence.</p></article><article class="card"><h2><a href="https://veritaschain.org/research/vcp-integrity/">VCP integrity, numeric representation and migration research</a></h2><p>Navigate known issues, proposed repairs, candidate schemas and synthetic tests without mixing their versions or adoption status.</p></article><article class="card"><h2><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vcp/sdk/">VCP SDK: source, installation and verification limits</a></h2><p>An offline core for Python, TypeScript and MQL5. Check distribution status, the installation snapshot and unsupported claims before evaluating it.</p></article></div><h2>Select the evaluation revision</h2><p>The offline evidence verifier and the Linux/Docker OS-isolation kit are separate. The interop signature-input fix is on main only; existing tags and fixed ZIPs do not contain it. Record the commit, inputs, trust, dependencies and support provided.</p><h2>Document status and historical records</h2><p>OAP, MAP, PAP Track B and DAP/SMP have registry states but unpublished texts. This directory does not invent unpublished specifications or adopt proposals.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/research/">VSO research directory and sources</a> · <a href="/updates/">Historical notices and test records</a></p><p class="note">Public-source review: 14 November 2026. Documentation navigation, not a new research test run.</p></section>
+</div></main>
